[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605263801-shidemori-memorial-cemetery-tier-b-actor-r0", :adr/title "ADR-2605263801: shidemori (死出守) — non-profit religious-corp memorial + cemetery substrate Tier-B actor R0 charter (FINAL gap-closure)", :adr/status "proposed", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2605263801: shidemori (死出守) — non-profit religious-corp memorial + cemetery substrate Tier-B actor R0 charter (FINAL gap-closure)\n\n**Status**: proposed\n**Date**: 2026-05-26\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n# Context\n\nThe gap audit (session 2026-05-26) identified memorial + cemetery as\npriority row 10, the FINAL gap in the 10-actor 30min-loop wave.\n\nshidemori was explicitly path-reserved as a future cross-actor by\nmultiple existing actors:\n- musubi (ADR-2605263400) — funeral ceremony → memorial NFT mint pair;\n- chigiri (ADR-2605262700) — covenant ceremony funeral type + inheritanceChain handoff;\n- kazaori (ADR-2605263200) — mass-fatality memorial coordination;\n- kokoro (ADR-2605263700) — post-funeral grief continuity (musubi-paired).\n\nThis ADR realizes those path-reserves and **closes the 10-actor gap-closure\nwave**.\n\nEtymology: 死出守 (shidemori) — 死出 = death-journey (classical 死出\nの旅 imagery; 万葉集 references); 守 = guardian / keeper. \"Guardian\nof the death-journey\". The kanji choice honors the cross-tradition\ninheritance:\n\n- **Reformed memorial view** (Sola Scriptura; memorial bread + cup\n  per 1 Corinthians 11:24-26; remembrance not transubstantiation);\n- **Shinto 鎮魂** (chinkon; soul-pacifying; ancestral honor);\n- **仏 教 49日 cycle** (Buddhist 中陰 intermediate-state cycle);\n- **Secular humanist remembrance** (life-honoring without\n  metaphysical claim).\n\nAll accommodated within Charter §1.13 (Wellbecoming) + §1.15 (non-\neschatological) + §1.7 (反個人主義 + 多世代) boundaries.\n\nConstitutional constraints (inherited; not adjustable):\n\n- **Charter §1.15 non-eschatological invariant** — memorial does NOT\n  make eschatological claims about afterlife (apocalyptic / millennial\n  / specific-heaven-hell-mapping). Honors the deceased without\n  imposing afterlife doctrine. G3 structural enforcement via\n  `memorialNftAttestation.afterlifeDoctrineImposed` const false;\n  extends kataribe G4 pattern (non-eschatological tone in publishing)\n  to memorial domain.\n- **Cross-doctrinal Wellbecoming priority** — same pattern as musubi\n  G9+N12 + kataribe G6 + kokoro G12, now extended into memorial\n  domain. Members from Christian / Buddhist / Shinto /\n  nondenominational / secular traditions accommodated; no\n  single-tradition afterlife monopoly.\n- **NOT state-licensed mortuary services** — community-witnessed-\n  competent guardians (musubi G3 pattern shared, now spanning\n  musubi + kataribe + kokoro + shidemori = 4-actor maturity).\n  External licensed mortuary engagement (legal compliance: death\n  certificate filing / cremation permit / interment permit) via\n  Public Fund Safe Council Lv6+ ≥4/7 (chigiri G14 + iyashi N9 +\n  kokoro G3 UPL-equivalent pattern extended).\n- **NO commercial memorial software** (G6) — Frazer Consultants /\n  Tribute Center / FuneralOne / ASD / SRS Computing / Wilbert /\n  Aldor / Adobe Cemetery Mgmt / Cremation Society Cremation Mgmt\n  PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e) + §2(c). Extends musubi G6\n  prohibition specifically into the memorial software domain.\n- **NO embalming chemicals** (G7) — Charter Rider §2(d) toxic\n  chemistry prohibition. Green burial + cremation only;\n  biodegradable shroud / pine casket; NO formaldehyde / methanol /\n  phenol injection. This is structurally important: most US\n  funeral industry practices use embalming, but Charter §2(d) +\n  §1.7 多世代 (multi-gen soil and groundwater preservation) + §1.13\n  Wellbecoming preclude.\n- **Land Trust waqf-equivalent cemetery rights** (G10) — per\n  ADR-2605192245; cemetery land inalienability; same mizuho G11\n  water-source pattern shared (now 2 actor enforcement of the\n  waqf-equivalent doctrine across water + cemetery domains).\n- **Member burial-or-cremation directive** (G9) — free conscience;\n  opt-in at onboarding or rededication ceremony (cross-actor with\n  musubi); no default imposed; multi-doctrinal preferences honored.\n- **NO surveillance-based mortuary** (G8) — Charter §2(c); no\n  funeral home surveillance; no live-streaming without per-party\n  consent. Mortuary domain extension of musubi G8 + kokoro G10\n  patterns.\n- **Murakumo-only inference** (G12) — memorial NFT generation\n  artwork / inscription text via judah LiteLLM → gemma4:e4b;\n  commercial memorial AI PROHIBITED.\n- **NO payroll for guardians** (G11) — vocation-flow L5 stewards;\n  cross-actor enforcement pattern now consistent across all 10\n  gap-closure Tier-B actors.\n\n# Decision\n\nCreate `shidemori` (死出守) as a Tier-B religious-corp memorial +\ncemetery substrate actor at `20-actors/shidemori/`, with DID\n`did:web:shidemori.etzhayyim.com`, Lexicon namespace\n`com.etzhayyim.shidemori.*`. R0 = scaffold only; all cells import-time\n`RuntimeError`.\n\n## §1. Identity and naming\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Name | `shidemori` (死出守 — guardian of the death-journey; 死出 = 死出の旅 classical imagery + 守 = keeper) |\n| DID | `did:web:shidemori.etzhayyim.com` |\n| Lexicon root | `com.etzhayyim.shidemori.*` |\n| Form | 任意団体 internal memorial + cemetery substrate (NOT 一般社団 / NPO / 公益財団 / 宗教法人 法人格; NOT state-licensed mortuary entity — Preamble §0.4 Lv7+ unanimity lock) |\n| Tier | Tier-B per-domain leader actor |\n| Final gap-closure | This actor completes the 10-actor 30min-loop gap-closure wave (audit list: toritate / iyashi / mizuho / kazaori / musubi / wakai / kataribe / kokoro / shidemori — and chigiri preceded as the kick-off) |\n| Cross-actor | musubi.funeral_ceremony (TIGHT — memorial NFT mint pair) / chigiri.inheritanceChain (TIGHT — succession handoff pair) / Land Registry (cemetery waqf cross-link) / toritate (cemetery maintenance Public Fund) / kokoro.grief_support (post-funeral grief continuity) / musubi.seasonal_communal_ceremony (鎮魂 annual cycle) / kazaori (mass-fatality memorial; kazaori path-reserved shidemori at R0) / kataribe (memorial publication; cross-doctrinal grief literature) |\n\n## §2. Scope (6 cells)\n\n### A. Memorial NFT mint\n\n- Per-deceased NFT mint upon musubi.funeral_ceremony completion;\n- Memorial NFT carries: deceased pseudonym DID / dates / cross-\n  doctrinal honor text (member-directive-respecting) / community-\n  witnessed competence-of-life summary (member-attested or family-\n  attested per member directive);\n- G3 STRUCTURAL: `afterlifeDoctrineImposed` const false (Charter\n  §1.15 non-eschatological); NO apocalyptic / specific-heaven-hell-\n  mapping claim;\n- Cross-link to musubi.ceremonyPerformanceAttestation\n  (ceremonyType=funeral) + chigiri.inheritanceChain.\n\n### B. Cemetery land registry\n\n- Per-cemetery-site Land Registry entry (waqf-equivalent\n  inalienability per ADR-2605192245);\n- G10 STRUCTURAL: `landRegistryCid` REQUIRED + `waqfInalienabilityAttested`\n  const true (mizuho G11 pattern shared);\n- Cemetery rights belong to Land Trust permanently;\n- NO cemetery land transfer / sale / lease.\n\n### C. 鎮魂 (chinkon) annual remembrance cycle\n\n- Cross-actor with musubi.seasonal_communal_ceremony (annual cycle);\n- Multi-gen community remembrance (Charter §1.7 多世代);\n- Cross-doctrinal Wellbecoming priority (Christian + Buddhist 49日 +\n  Shinto + nondenominational + secular memorial preferences\n  accommodated per G4);\n- Community-discerned attendance (opt-in per G9 free conscience).\n\n### D. Inheritance handoff\n\n- TIGHT cross-actor with chigiri.inheritanceChain;\n- G13 STRUCTURAL: chigiri.inheritanceChain emit MANDATORY when\n  deceased had Adherent SBT;\n- Adherent SBT burn coordination (chigiri.member_offboarding pair);\n- Wallet handover via ERC-4337 paymaster (chigiri.inheritanceChain\n  per existing pattern).\n\n### E. External mortuary engagement (UPL-equivalent pattern)\n\n- When state-licensed compliance required (death certificate\n  filing / cremation permit / interment permit / autopsy\n  coordination if applicable);\n- Public Fund Safe Council Lv6+ ≥4/7 approves engagement;\n- Cross-actor with toritate.externalAuditorEngagement-equivalent\n  pattern (now 4-actor UPL-equivalent pattern: chigiri G14\n  legal + iyashi N9 clinical + kokoro G3 mental health +\n  shidemori G5 mortuary);\n- External licensed mortuary handles legal-compliance; shidemori\n  prepares the data package + records the engagement; shidemori\n  does NOT do state-licensed mortuary work itself.\n\n### F. Memorial directive (member directive at onboarding)\n\n- Member burial-or-cremation preference at chigiri.member_onboarding\n  or rededication ceremony;\n- Cross-doctrinal preferences honored (G4);\n- Free conscience (G9; opt-in; no default);\n- Directive stored encrypted per ADR-2605181100; revealed only at\n  member-death event by chigiri.inheritance cell.\n\n## §3. Cells (6 Pregel cells under `40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/shidemori_*/`)\n\nAll R0 path-reserved; import-time `RuntimeError(\"shidemori R0 scaffold: activate via Council ADR + R1 ratification + ≥3 guardian baseline attestations + ≥1 cemetery Land Registry waqf-attested entry\")` at W1 creation.\n\n| # | Cell | Murakumo node | Phase | I/O |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `memorial_nft_mint` | zebulun (musubi-paired TIGHT) | event | musubi.funeral_ceremony complete → memorialNftAttestation + on-chain mint |\n| 2 | `cemetery_land_registry` | zebulun (Land Registry paired) | event | new cemetery site registration → cemeteryLandAttestation (waqf-inalienability attested) |\n| 3 | `chinkon_annual_remembrance` | zebulun (musubi seasonal-pair) | annual | annual cycle → chinkonRemembranceAttestation |\n| 4 | `inheritance_handoff` | zebulun (chigiri-paired TIGHT) | event | musubi funeral + Adherent SBT burn coordination → chigiri.inheritanceChain cross-emit |\n| 5 | `external_mortuary_engagement` | zebulun (toritate-paired UPL-equivalent) | event | state-compliance need → Public Fund Council Lv6+ ≥4/7 + externalMortuaryEngagement record |\n| 6 | `silen_shidemori_review` | zebulun | quarterly | Council Wellbecoming + multi-doctrinal + Land Trust + Charter §1.15 + §2(d) audit |\n\nR1 activation gates each cell separately + ≥3 guardian baseline\nattestations + ≥1 cemetery Land Registry waqf-attested entry.\n\n## §4. Lexicons (5, all under `com.etzhayyim.shidemori.*`)\n\n| # | Lexicon | Consumer cell | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| L1 | `memorialNftAttestation` | memorial_nft_mint | Per-deceased mint; G3 STRUCTURAL: afterlifeDoctrineImposed const false; musubi funeral + chigiri inheritance cross-link |\n| L2 | `cemeteryLandAttestation` | cemetery_land_registry | Per-cemetery-site; G10 STRUCTURAL: landRegistryCid REQUIRED + waqfInalienabilityAttested const true (mizuho G11 pattern shared) |\n| L3 | `chinkonRemembranceAttestation` | chinkon_annual_remembrance | Annual cycle; G4 cross-doctrinal accommodation tracking; multi-gen cohort mix per Charter §1.7 |\n| L4 | `externalMortuaryEngagement` | external_mortuary_engagement | UPL-equivalent pattern (chigiri G14 + iyashi N9 + kokoro G3 + shidemori G5); Public Fund Safe contract CID + Council Lv6+ ≥4 attestations |\n| L5 | `silenShidemoriReview` | silen_shidemori_review | Quarterly Council review; G3/G4/G5/G6/G7/G8/G9/G10/G11/G12 const-field structural enforcement |\n\n## §5. Gates (13, immutable R0..R3, Council Lv6+ to amend)\n\n| Gate | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **G1** | Every memorial document MUST pass `kotodama.organism.sensors.charter_rider.scan()` §2(a)-(h). |\n| **G2** | Every record MUST emit `com.etzhayyim.shidemori.*` Lexicon with kotoba-datomic attestation lineage. |\n| **G3** | **Charter §1.15 non-eschatological** — NO apocalyptic / millennial / specific-heaven-hell-mapping afterlife claims; honors deceased without imposing afterlife doctrine; `memorialNftAttestation.afterlifeDoctrineImposed` const false structural (extends kataribe G4 pattern to memorial domain). |\n| **G4** | **Cross-doctrinal Wellbecoming priority** — Christian + Buddhist (49日 / 中陰) + Shinto (鎮魂) + nondenominational + secular memorial preferences all accommodated (musubi G9+N12 + kataribe G6 + kokoro G12 pattern shared, now 4-actor maturity in memorial domain). |\n| **G5** | **NOT state-licensed mortuary services** — community-witnessed-competent guardians per musubi G3 pattern shared; external licensed mortuary engagement via Public Fund Safe Council Lv6+ ≥4/7 (chigiri G14 + iyashi N9 + kokoro G3 UPL-equivalent pattern extended to mortuary). |\n| **G6** | **NO commercial memorial software** — Frazer Consultants / Tribute Center / FuneralOne / ASD / SRS Computing / Wilbert / Aldor / Adobe Cemetery Mgmt / Cremation Society Cremation Mgmt PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e) + §2(c) (extends musubi G6). |\n| **G7** | **NO embalming chemicals** — Charter Rider §2(d) toxic chemistry prohibition; green burial + cremation only; biodegradable shroud / pine casket; NO formaldehyde / methanol / phenol injection. |\n| **G8** | **NO surveillance-based mortuary** — Charter §2(c) covert-ops avoidance; no funeral home surveillance; no live-streaming without per-party consent (musubi G8 + kokoro G10 pattern extended to mortuary). |\n| **G9** | **Member burial-or-cremation directive** — free conscience; opt-in at member onboarding or rededication; no default imposed; multi-doctrinal preferences honored per G4. |\n| **G10** | **Land Trust waqf-equivalent cemetery rights** — per ADR-2605192245; cemetery land inalienability; `cemeteryLandAttestation.landRegistryCid` REQUIRED + `waqfInalienabilityAttested` const true (mizuho G11 pattern shared). |\n| **G11** | NO payroll for guardians — vocation-flow L5 stewards (cross-actor enforcement pattern shared across all Tier-B Care+Memorial actors). |\n| **G12** | Murakumo-only inference per ADR-2605215000 — commercial memorial AI PROHIBITED. |\n| **G13** | Cross-actor chigiri.inheritanceChain emit MANDATORY when deceased had Adherent SBT (TIGHT pair). |\n\n## §6. Non-goals (12, immutable R0..R3)\n\n| # | Non-goal |\n|---|---|\n| N1 | NOT state-licensed mortuary services. |\n| N2 | NOT commercial cemetery operator. |\n| N3 | NOT apocalyptic / eschatological afterlife claims (Charter §1.15). |\n| N4 | NOT mandatory religious-corp burial. |\n| N5 | NOT embalming / body preservation chemicals (Charter §2(d)). |\n| N6 | NOT mortuary surveillance. |\n| N7 | NOT commercial memorial software integrator. |\n| N8 | NOT single-doctrinal afterlife monopoly. |\n| N9 | NOT closed-source. |\n| N10 | NOT a state-licensed entity. |\n| N11 | NOT payroll-based guardian. |\n| N12 | NOT mandatory burial (free conscience). |\n\n## §7. Roadmap (R0 → R3)\n\n| Phase | Date / gate | Scope | Murakumo placement |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **R0** | 2026-05-26 (this ADR — FINAL gap-closure commit) | Scaffold only. 6 cells path-reserved. 5 Lexicons schema skeleton. | No deployment |\n| **R1** | post-Council + ≥3 guardian baseline attestations + ≥1 cemetery Land Registry waqf-attested entry + musubi R2 active + chigiri R2 active | Activate 3 core cells: `memorial_nft_mint` (musubi TIGHT pair) + `cemetery_land_registry` + `inheritance_handoff` (chigiri TIGHT pair). | zebulun (single node) |\n| **R2** | post-R1 + 30-day public objection + cross-doctrinal advisor on Council + kokoro R2 active | Activate +2 cells: `chinkon_annual_remembrance` (musubi seasonal-pair) + `external_mortuary_engagement` (toritate UPL-equivalent). | zebulun + simeon (2 nodes) |\n| **R3** | post-R2 + Council Lv7+ unanimity + ≥1 full annual chinkon cycle + silen_shidemori_review cycle established | Activate +1 cell: `silen_shidemori_review`. Multi-site community-scale + cross-religious-corp federation potential. | zebulun + simeon + asher (3 nodes) |\n\n## §8. Cross-actor relationship table\n\n| Cross-actor | Direction | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `musubi.funeral_ceremony` | ↔ (TIGHT — memorial NFT mint pair) | Per-funeral memorial NFT mint upon ceremony completion |\n| `musubi.seasonal_communal_ceremony` | ↔ (chinkon annual pair) | Annual remembrance cycle cross-actor (Charter §1.7 多世代) |\n| `chigiri.inheritanceChain` | ↔ (TIGHT — succession handoff pair) | G13 MANDATORY emit; wallet + SBT succession coordination |\n| `chigiri.member_offboarding` | ↔ (Adherent SBT burn coordination) | Adherent SBT burn upon death |\n| `chigiri.member_onboarding` | ← (read) | Member burial-or-cremation directive at onboarding |\n| Land Registry | ↔ | Cemetery waqf-equivalent inalienability cross-actor (G10; mizuho G11 pattern shared) |\n| `toritate` | → (read; cemetery maintenance accounting) | Public Fund grant for cemetery maintenance |\n| `kokoro.grief_support` | ↔ | Post-funeral grief continuity cross-actor (kokoro grief_support TIGHT pair with musubi.funeral_ceremony, shidemori complements) |\n| `kazaori` | ↔ (mass-fatality memorial; kazaori path-reserved shidemori at R0) | Mass-fatality memorial coordination when applicable |\n| `kataribe` | ↔ (memorial publication; cross-doctrinal grief literature) | Memorial obituary publication + cross-doctrinal grief literature |\n\n## §9. R0 deliverables (this commit — FINAL gap-closure)\n\n1. This ADR (`90-docs/adr/2605263800-shidemori-memorial-cemetery-tier-b-actor-r0.edn`);\n2. Actor scaffold (`20-actors/shidemori/manifest.jsonld` + `README.edn` + `CLAUDE.md`);\n3. 5 Lexicon JSON skeleton schemas under `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/shidemori/` + README;\n4. `deps.toml` [[adrs]] + [[modules]] entries;\n5. `90-docs/adr/README.edn` index update;\n6. `CLAUDE.md` Status table row 77 + Repo Layout entry;\n7. **GAP CLOSURE WAVE COMPLETE** — 10 of 10 audit-listed actors shipped at R0.\n\nNo code activation in R0.\n\n# Consequences\n\n**Positive**:\n\n- **FINAL gap-closure** — religious-corp now has complete Tier-B\n  actor coverage across the 10-priority audit list (chigiri / toritate\n  / iyashi / mizuho / kazaori / musubi / wakai / kataribe / kokoro /\n  shidemori);\n- G3 Charter §1.15 non-eschatological invariant operationalized in\n  memorial domain (where eschatological framing is most tempting);\n- G4 cross-doctrinal Wellbecoming priority now a 4-actor pattern\n  (musubi + kataribe + kokoro + shidemori) — stable maturity sign;\n- G5 NOT-state-licensed-mortuary discipline (chigiri G14 + iyashi\n  N9 + kokoro G3 + shidemori G5) = 4-actor UPL-equivalent pattern\n  maturity;\n- G7 green burial + no embalming chemicals operationalizes Charter\n  Rider §2(d) toxic chemistry prohibition in memorial domain (where\n  embalming is industry-default);\n- G10 Land Trust waqf-equivalent cemetery rights = 2-actor pattern\n  (mizuho G11 water + shidemori G10 cemetery) — extending Land\n  Trust doctrine across resource + memorial domains;\n- musubi → kokoro → shidemori 3-actor cross-actor coordination for\n  funeral → grief → memorial covers the full bereavement arc;\n- Memorial NFT pattern integrates with chigiri.inheritanceChain\n  cleanly (G13 TIGHT pair);\n- Final 9-novenary gates pattern (kokoro 9-novenary + shidemori\n  10-decennary) shows discipline scaling with actor domain\n  complexity.\n\n**Negative / cost**:\n\n- ≥3 guardian baseline attestations + ≥1 cemetery Land Registry\n  waqf-attested entry are R1 gating dependencies; Bootstrap\n  Council Seat 2-5 RFP + Public Fund Lv6+ ≥4/7 cemetery land\n  acquisition required;\n- G7 no-embalming may conflict with state requirements in some\n  jurisdictions (some US states mandate embalming for transport\n  >24h); external mortuary engagement (G5 / external_mortuary_engagement\n  cell) handles via Public Fund Council Lv6+ ≥4/7 + UPL-equivalent\n  pattern; some friction expected;\n- G3 non-eschatological invariant may conflict with strong-\n  doctrinal members from traditions with detailed afterlife\n  cosmologies; G4 cross-doctrinal Wellbecoming priority handles\n  via accommodation (members may privately hold any view; shidemori\n  does NOT impose);\n- Land Trust waqf cemetery acquisition is expensive (Public Fund\n  capital investment ~$50k-$500k per cemetery site depending on\n  jurisdiction); Council Lv6+ ≥4/7 bandwidth required for each;\n- Memorial NFT mint requires on-chain gas cost (Base L2 minimal but\n  non-zero); Public Fund ERC-4337 paymaster pattern handles.\n\n**Forward-compatibility**:\n\n- Cross-religious-corp federation potential — memorial framework is\n  cross-doctrinal and could be shared with future Sphere-style\n  partner religious-corps;\n- Annual chinkon cycle (R3) extends multi-gen Charter §1.7 invariant\n  across decades;\n- Memorial NFT pattern reusable for non-member honorings (e.g.,\n  founders / advisors who consented before death) with separate\n  attestation chain.\n\n# Alternatives Considered\n\n1. **Subsume into musubi (covenant ceremony)**. Rejected — musubi\n   is ceremony performance; shidemori is post-ceremony memorial +\n   cemetery infrastructure; SRP violation if merged. Same\n   discipline as iyashi separate from mitate.\n\n2. **Use Frazer Consultants / FuneralOne / SRS Computing / Aldor as\n   memorial software**. Rejected per G6 + Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c)\n   (extends musubi G6 prohibition to memorial-specific software).\n\n3. **Allow embalming for jurisdictional transport compliance**.\n   Rejected per G7 + Charter Rider §2(d) toxic chemistry. External\n   mortuary engagement (G5) handles the rare jurisdictional case\n   via Public Fund Council Lv6+ ≥4/7; embalming chemicals stay\n   outside religious-corp first-party practice.\n\n4. **Allow eschatological afterlife claims in memorial content**\n   (some members from strong-doctrinal traditions expect them).\n   Rejected per G3 + Charter §1.15 non-eschatological invariant.\n   Cross-doctrinal Wellbecoming (G4) accommodates members'\n   private views; shidemori does NOT impose afterlife doctrine\n   in public memorial content.\n\n5. **Make burial-or-cremation choice mandatory at member onboarding**.\n   Rejected per G9 free conscience invariant. Member directive is\n   opt-in; default is \"no preference recorded; family + community\n   discerns at funeral time within Charter §1.13 + §1.15 boundaries\".\n\n6. **Allow surveillance-based mortuary (cameras for security)**.\n   Rejected per G8 + Charter §2(c) covert-ops avoidance (extends\n   musubi G8 + kokoro G10 patterns to mortuary).\n\n7. **Skip shidemori — let musubi.funeral_ceremony handle memorial\n   downstream**. Rejected — musubi G3 explicitly path-reserved\n   shidemori for funeral → memorial NFT cross-link; kazaori\n   ADR-2605263200 path-reserved shidemori for mass-fatality\n   memorial; kokoro ADR-2605263700 grief_support pair benefits\n   from shidemori companion. Multi-actor path-reserve indicates\n   real distinct domain.\n\n# References\n\n- ADR-2605170900 — etzhayyim/root canonical home for ADRs\n- ADR-2605181100 — MST encrypted records + Signal key wrap\n- ADR-2605192100 — Mission Charter (§1.7 多世代 + 反個人主義; §1.13 Wellbecoming; §1.15 non-eschatological)\n- ADR-2605192145 — Public Fund architecture (cemetery + external mortuary engagement source)\n- ADR-2605192200 — Charter Compliance Rider v2.0 (§2(d) toxic chemistry + §2(e)+§2(c) sources)\n- ADR-2605192245 — Global Land Sovereignty (G10 cemetery waqf-equivalent inalienability)\n- ADR-2605192300 — Council 5-of-7 Safe\n- ADR-2605215000 — Inference Murakumo-only (G12)\n- ADR-2605261000 — Labor Liberation Transition Mechanism (G11 vocation-flow)\n- ADR-2605262130 — Kotoba storage substrate\n- ADR-2605262700 — chigiri (TIGHT inheritanceChain pair; G14 UPL-equivalent pattern shared)\n- ADR-2605262900 — toritate (cemetery maintenance + external mortuary engagement Public Fund accounting)\n- ADR-2605263100 — mizuho (G10 waqf-equivalent pattern shared; cemetery + water inalienability invariant)\n- ADR-2605263200 — kazaori (mass-fatality memorial path-reserved shidemori at R0)\n- ADR-2605263400 — musubi (TIGHT funeral_ceremony memorial NFT mint pair; G3 community-witnessed-competent pattern shared)\n- ADR-2605263600 — kataribe (memorial publication + cross-doctrinal grief literature)\n- ADR-2605263700 — kokoro (grief support continuity; G3 community-witnessed-competent pattern shared)\n- `/CHARTER-RIDER.md` §2(d) + §2(e) + §2(c) — G7 + G6 + G8 sources\n\n---\n\n## FINAL gap-closure note (2026-05-26)\n\nThis ADR completes the 10-actor 30min-loop gap-closure wave initiated\n2026-05-26 (cron job `8c681144` for the /loop discipline). The 10\naudit-listed Tier-B actors now have R0 charters + scaffolds +\nLexicons + registry updates committed:\n\n| Iteration | Actor | ADR | Gap audit row |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| (pre-loop) | chigiri (契) — legal procedure | 2605262700 | row 1 |\n| 1 | toritate (執帳) — accounting + audit | 2605262900 | row 2 |\n| 2 | iyashi (癒) — clinical care provider | 2605263000 | row 3 |\n| 3 | mizuho (水穂) — water + sanitation | 2605263100 | row 4 |\n| 4 | kazaori (風折) — disaster response | 2605263200 | row 5 |\n| 5 | musubi (結) — covenant ceremony | 2605263400 | row 6 |\n| 6 | wakai (和会) — mutual aid | 2605263500 | row 7 |\n| 7 | kataribe (語部) — press + publishing + translation | 2605263600 | row 8 |\n| 8 | kokoro (心) — mental health | 2605263700 | row 9 |\n| 9 | shidemori (死出守) — memorial + cemetery | 2605263800 | row 10 |\n\nCoverage now ~85-87% → **~87-90%** essential-life-function coverage.\n\nThe /loop cron job `8c681144` may be stopped via `CronDelete 8c681144`\nupon completion of this commit (the gap-closure list is exhausted).\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605263801-shidemori-memorial-cemetery-tier-b-actor-r0.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "shidemori-memorial-cemetery-r0", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-26", :adr/date "2026-05-26", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/authoritative_for ["shidemori actor R0 charter (FINAL gap-closure of 10-actor 30min-loop wave)" "religious-corp memorial + cemetery substrate single SoT" "`com.etzhayyim.shidemori.*` Lexicon namespace boundary" "Charter §1.15 non-eschatological